installed `ON DELETE SET NULL` FK needs to update that conversation. Each transaction can wait for the other. One is 
aborted with `40P01`, which these routes return as 500. The headerâ€™s â€œno lock cycleâ€ claim overlooks implicit FK 
writes. [PostgreSQL locking documentation](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/explicit-locking.html)

   **Smallest fix:** make the transactional space-delete path lock affected conversations before deleting the space, 
and audit other parent deletions for implicit FK locks. Add a held join/delete integration test.

