3:Revision: migration supabase/migrations/20261007184118_conversation_membership_integrity.sql revised in place 
(rolled back with its header SQL and reapplied locally); test 
__tests__/messaging-db/conversation-membership-integrity.test.ts (37 tests). No application code, function body, 
policy, grant, or rollback-SQL change in this round.
4:Performer's claims: (1) opening locks are now `lock table public.users in exclusive mode nowait;` then `lock table 
public.conversations, public.conversation_members in access exclusive mode nowait;` — the migration fails at once with 
55P03 on any contention, before changing anything, so it never waits behind (and never deadlocks with) an application 
transaction; EXCLUSIVE (not SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE) on users so a FOR UPDATE row-lock holder (ROW SHARE) also makes it 
fail fast instead of the backfill's FK check waiting; header lock-order claims corrected (application paths take these 
tables in both orders) and the operator procedure documented: re-run the whole file until it applies, at low traffic; 
autovacuum (ShareUpdateExclusiveLock) can also cause 55P03 (diagnosed with a stress script: 2 refusals in 1255 
attempts, holder autovacuum VACUUM ANALYZE). Regressions run the LOCK lines exactly as read from the migration file in 
a rolled-back transaction: a held read-state transaction (members updated, then mark_conversation_read takes the FK 
lock on conversations) → locks fail 55P03 < 1 s, the reader commits; a users row FOR UPDATE holder → 55P03, holder 
commits; Presence holding a user while join_room_conversation waits → 55P03, both commit, membership exists; each 
re-run modelled as bounded re-attempts (≤10 × 200 ms, every refusal must be 55P03). Init-race script still shows the 
r1 #2 guarantee (DELETE in flight → apply fails with 0 history rows, re-run backfills the revocation; migration open → 
DELETE waits and the trigger records it). (2) header "Backward compatible" paragraph now states the inherited 
limitation: hosted build e27dd10 creates with INSERT … RETURNING and is refused 403/42501 when users.id ≠ 
supabase_uid, identically on the pre-T28 database. Tests: membership file 37/37 in 6 + 3 consecutive runs, messaging 
DB 145/145, type-check clean.
5:Verify both r2 fixes; attack: whether any statement after the two locks can still wait on an application lock (FK 
checks on other tables, e.g. spaces/companies referenced by the backfill or triggers; catalog/DDL locks on other 
relations touched by CREATE TRIGGER/POLICY/FUNCTION or GRANT), whether NOWAIT + ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on 
conversations/conversation_members during a busy period can starve indefinitely or hurt the online apply procedure 
(PLAN T23 standing method applies each file transactionally), whether the test's bounded re-attempt weakens what it 
proves, and every claim in the revised header. Keep r1 resolutions in view.
